    <div>
      <span class="tlabel">Tier II</span>
      <h2>The <strong>strategy</strong></h2>
      <p class="tsum">Vision becomes direction through a few commitments: the worship we build, the people we build, and how we operate. Each one grows out of an Orbit value.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="block" id="worship-we-build">
    <h3>The worship we build</h3>
    <p class="lead">Four marks. Every set, every song, every Sunday is measured against them.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><div class="lbl">01</div><h4>Excellent</h4><p>We pursue excellence so the room can forget we are here. It is hospitality, not performance. We bring our best even on our off days.</p><span class="from">From: We are ON on our off days</span></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="lbl">02</div><h4>Christ-Centered</h4><p>Every choice points to Jesus and stands on His Word, never on us or a vague spirituality. We revolve everything around Him.</p><span class="from">From: We put God's Word in our world</span></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="lbl">03</div><h4>Real</h4><p>We worship for real before we ask anyone to follow. No performing, no pretending. We offer what we actually have, honestly.</p><span class="from">From: We work with what we have</span></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="lbl">04</div><h4>Creative</h4><p>We imagine more of what God could do through worship and production, and keep reaching for it. The Orbit Sound is built here.</p><span class="from">From: We imagine more</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="people-we-build">
    <h3>The people we build</h3>
    <p class="lead">Those four marks only ever show up through a certain kind of person. We build two things into everyone.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><div class="lbl">05</div><h4>High Skill</h4><p>We get good on purpose. Skill is how excellence and creativity become real, and it is a gift to the room. We teach it forward instead of hoarding it.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="lbl">06</div><h4>High Character</h4><p>Who you are offstage is who you are. The platform reveals character, it does not build it. Humility and obedience are the standard, on the stage and off it.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="how-we-operate">
    <h3>How we operate</h3>
    <p class="lead">A few operating commitments shape everything at the base.</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li><strong>Plan far, hold loose.</strong> We aim to sit two quarters ahead and refine every quarter. Margin lets us minister on Sunday instead of scrambling, and hold the set loosely enough to follow the room.</li>
      <li><strong>Equip, don't hoard.</strong> A skill that lives in only one person is a liability. We spread it across the team on purpose.</li>
      <li><strong>Work with what we have.</strong> We are portable. We build the room and tear it down every week, and we steward the people and gear God has given us instead of waiting on better.</li>
      <li><strong>Start stuff.</strong> Purpose takes initiative. We keep launching what serves the vision.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where "start stuff" is taking us</h3>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li><strong>Worship Nights.</strong> Time set apart to seek God, where the Orbit Sound gets room to breathe.</li>
      <li><strong>Youth Worship.</strong> Raising up the next room of worshipers.</li>
      <li><strong>Songwriting and original music.</strong> Writing out of this house and recording it, so the Orbit Sound outlives a single Sunday.</li>
      <li><strong>Leaders.</strong> A real pipeline where apprentices grow into leads.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="strip dark"><span class="mk">GUARDING THE VISION</span><p>Ideas are welcome from anyone, and we want them. The one condition is that a change has to move us toward this vision, not away from it. Efficiency and preference do not get to quietly redirect the mission. We would rather be slow and aligned than fast and drifting.</p></div>
  </section>
</div>

